{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And Abraham rose early in the morning and took bread and a skin of water.</b> He should have given her silver and gold and camels to carry them, according to the abundance of wealth that was in Abraham's house, for he was his son, concerning whom he had prayed over him, 'let Ishmael live before You.' But because Sarah said to him that he should cast out him and his mother, and HaShem said to Abraham, 'whatever Sarah says to you, listen to her voice' — therefore he listened to Sarah's voice and cast him and his mother out with bread and a skin of water. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory." "<b>It is fitting</b> to say that the reason he cast him out with bread and water includes another matter, namely that Abraham saw in the vision of prophecy that his descendants were destined to be subjugated under the hand of Ishmael, and that they would hate them with a great hatred, such that there is no nation in the world that hates Israel like the children of Ishmael — therefore Abraham conducted himself toward him as one ought to conduct himself toward an enemy, and gave him bread and water, as it is written (Proverbs 25:21): ״אם רעב שונאך האכילהו לחם ואם צמא השקהו מים״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:58.670586101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}